5. PROHIBITED USES

The Materials must not be used, directly or indirectly, to cause, enable, facilitate, encourage, or materially increase the risk of harm.

Prohibited uses include unauthorized access, scanning, exploitation, interference, or disruption; malware, ransomware, destructive code, credential theft, phishing, fraud, impersonation, or malicious evasion; offensive cyber operations or testing without explicit lawful authority and documented authorization; unlawful surveillance, coercion, harassment, discrimination, manipulation, or infringement of rights; unsafe or reckless use; unlawful processing or disclosure of sensitive information; targeting safety-critical services without authorization and safeguards; or bypassing legal, ethical, safety, security, governance, or accountability controls for an unauthorized or harmful purpose.

